  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through next Monday)\nIssued at 218 PM CDT Mon Aug 24 2026\n\nUpper level ridge shifts back to the west for mid week, placing\nWest Central Texas in northerly flow aloft and allowing for a weak\nshortwave to rotate south across the area. Earlier models were a\nlittle more aggressive than the 12Z runs with showers and\nthunderstorm chances, but some scattered activity still looks\nlikely. These storms not likely to be severe but some gusty winds\nalways possible with convection during the summer months, just due\nto the invereted-V soundings if nothing else.\n\nWith the cloud cover in place and a weak surface boundary pushing\nthrough the area, highs on Thursday will be a little cooler. This\nmay be Abilene's chance to break the consecutive 100 degree\nstreak. After that, dry conditions return as the high pressure\nridge builds back once again. May not be hitting 105+ like this\nlast week, but highs near or a few degrees above the 100 degree\nmark look likely.",
